      },
      "text": "Dimensionless numbers arise from Buckingham Pi theorem: any physically meaningful equation can be restated in terms of dimensionless groups. Systems with identical dimensionless groups (Re, Pr, Nu) exhibit identical physics regardless of absolute scale — this is why wind tunnel models work. The groups collapse the parameter space: instead of varying velocity, density, viscosity, and length independently, we need only vary Re."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-HEAT-TRANSFER.md#035",
      "path": [
        "03-HEAT-TRANSFER.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
